---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const LINKEDIN = "https://www.linkedin.com/in/sekhar-nalla-2bb46763/";
const EMAIL = "nalla.sekhar90@gmail.com";
---

<Base title="About" description="About Sekhar Nalla — a mobile platform engineer focused on Android, Kotlin Multiplatform, CI/CD, and AI-augmented developer productivity.">
  <section class="about-page section">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="about-title">Mobile platform engineer focused on delivery systems and shared platforms.</h1>

      <div class="about-body">
        <p>
          I'm Sekhar Nalla, a Lead Mobile Software Engineer based in San Jose, CA. Over the
          past 12+ years I've built and scaled Android applications — from early
          GoToMeeting/GoToWebinar work at Citrix and LogMeIn, through modernizing large
          consumer mobile systems, to leading Kotlin Multiplatform platform strategy at Gen.
        </p>
        <p>
          My core work sits at the intersection of three things:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Mobile platform architecture</strong> — designing modular, independently versioned Kotlin Multiplatform feature SDKs shared between Android and iOS, with clean native UI boundaries and shared networking cores.</li>
          <li><strong>Engineering productivity &amp; CI/CD</strong> — multi-repository release engineering, change-aware pipelines, remote Gradle build caching, and observability. The result I'm proudest of is a 53% reduction in mobile CI duration.</li>
          <li><strong>AI-augmented delivery</strong> — agent workflows that automate release orchestration, failed PR-check remediation, dependency updates, and maestro-cli-based reproduce-and-verify loops.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          I care about the systems that make software delivery fast, reliable, and observable
          across teams — not just the features that ship on top of them. Lately I've been
          especially interested in how AI agents can remove manual toil from release and
          quality workflows without sacrificing safety or human judgment where it matters.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outside of work, I explore developer tooling, learn through hands-on experiments
          and technical talks, and enjoy discovering different hikes across the Bay Area
          and Marin County.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-cta">
        <h2 class="about-sub">Let's connect</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          I'm always happy to connect and talk about mobile technologies, Android
          engineering, Kotlin Multiplatform, and AI-enabled developer productivity.
        </p>
        <div class="about-links">
          <a href={EMAIL ? `mailto:${EMAIL}` : "#"} class="btn btn-primary">{EMAIL}</a>
          <a href={LINKEDIN} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="btn btn-ghost">LinkedIn</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-title {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .about-body {
    margin-top: var(--space-10);
  }
  .about-body p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .about-body ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin: var(--space-5) 0;
  }
  .about-body li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 66ch;
  }
  .about-body li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.55em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-primary);
  }
  .about-cta {
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .about-sub {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
  }
  .about-cta .muted {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .about-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
</style>
